Each monotonic-stack function processes every index once. Although elements may be popped inside the loops, each element is pushed and popped at most once per function.

There are four stack traversals:

- `findPSEE`
- `findNSE`
- `findPGEE`
- `findNGE`

Each takes `O(n)`, so the overall complexity remains:

```text
